+# Story RC3.4: Form Completion & Exit Routes — Submit, Decline, Objection (stop), Wrong Person
+
+**Status:** ready-for-dev (pending clarify confirmations below)
+**Epic:** RC3 (the referee collection funnel). Depends on RC3.3 (#596, merged).
+**Model:** `zai-coding-cn/glm-5.2` (kimi quota down this cycle; proven capable fallback).
+**Perkins:** ON (code — referee-facing exits + deterministic result; round runs on glm-5.2).
+**GitHub issue:** #548
+
+## Story
+
+> As a referee,
+> I want to submit my reference — or decline, object, or flag wrong details — and then be left alone,
+> So that taking part is my choice and stopping is instant.
+
+rc3-3 shipped the referee form *session* (`/reference/:token` — open, answer, autosave, resume, all-answered review whose Submit button is a forward link rc3-3 deliberately left 404ing). rc3-4 ships **everything that happens when the referee finishes or bails**: the deterministic submit path, the three honest exit routes, their notifications, and the thank-you screen. Every exit is honoured instantly and truthfully.
+
+## Scope (what THIS story owns — and what it does NOT)
+
+### OWNS
+1. **`POST /reference/:token`** — submit: validate every required answer, structure the deterministic `ReferenceCallResult v1` (AD-9), guarded `contact_initiated → form_completed` (AD-14), write `result` + denormalised `fraud_signals`, stamp `purge_after` from the application's `retention_due_at`, audit terminal entry, dispatch `reference_completed`, render the §6.5 thank-you. A second POST → branded "already completed" state (one submission, AD-3).
+2. **`GET|POST /reference/:token/decline`** — decline: GET renders the decline page (optional one-line reason, never required); POST guarded-transitions to `refused` (A8), writes a result per §4.6 (outcome + attempts, null `verification`), dispatches `reference_declined`, renders the §10.2 decline confirmation. All messages stop.
+3. **`GET|POST /reference/:token/stop`** — the stop-link (AD-6, the 2026-08-08 amendment): GET renders a pre-fetch-safe confirm page (link scanners mutate nothing); POST guarded-transitions to sticky `objected`, NULLs `next_attempt_at`, writes a `reference_objection_log` row at tap time (`channel: 'web'`, single writer), dispatches `reference_objected`, renders the §10.2 objection confirmation. A re-tap on an already-terminal token renders the branded terminal page (guarded UPDATE is a no-op).
+4. **`GET|POST /reference/:token/wrong-person`** — wrong-person: GET renders the wrong-person page; POST guarded-transitions to `awaiting_correction` (AD-7), NULLs `next_attempt_at` (never a re-send to the same details), renders the §10.2 wrong-person confirmation. No notification (the landlord sees the state in RC4).
+5. **`server/src/reference_checks/result.gleam`** (NEW) — the deterministic `ReferenceCallResult v1` structuring: draft → `verification` block per-slot (§5.3/A9), `free_text_signals` verbatim, deterministic `ai_summary` (headline/summary renderings of the verification block, completeness-derived `confidence`), `compliance` block, `attempts[]`, `outcome`, `schema_version:"refcall-v1"`, `channel:"form"`.
+6. **Notifications** — `notify_reference_completed` / `notify_reference_declined` / `notify_reference_objected` in `notification/notification_dispatch.gleam`, dispatched through the existing `dispatch()`/`maybe_send_email()` respecting `notification_preference`. Copy per §7.9 verbatim (modulo the em-dash ban).
+7. **Thank-you + 3 confirmation screens** in `form_pages.gleam` (`view_thank_you`, `view_decline_confirm`, `view_stop_confirm`, `view_wrong_person_confirm` + the GET confirm pages).
+8. **The `reference_objection_log.channel` migration** — extend the CHECK to include `'web'` (the AD-6 amendment updated §4.1's doc but the `20260731222000` migration lags; expand-only, single-deploy safe).
+9. **`update_reference_call_status.sql`** — add `awaiting_correction` to the `next_attempt_at = NULL` CASE list (AD-7: wrong-person must stop re-sends to the bad contact).
+10. **`get_form_context_by_form_token.sql`** — extend the SELECT with `v.user_id AS landlord_id` + `a.vacancy_id AS vacancy_id` (the join already touches those tables; notification dispatch needs them). Regenerate via Squirrel.
+11. **Route registration** — add the router arms; **verify** the three security registries (`is_public_path`, `csrf.should_skip`, `redact_token_route`) cover the new routes via their existing `["reference", ..]` prefix match, and **pin that coverage with tests** (the rc3-3 csrf-registry-completeness lens-guard's concern). No per-arm registry edits — the prefix match is the intentional design.
+12. **Carry-forward from rc3-3 r2** (APPROVED, 0 blockers, the advisory notes touching the files this story extends):
+    - **N3**: delete `form_handler.get_value`, route its call sites through `application_handler.get_form_value` (the local copy omits the trim — drift hazard).
+    - **N6**: extract `view_resend_form(token, button_label, form_testid, button_testid)` in `form_pages.gleam`; `view_expired` + `view_resend_failed` pass their distinct testids/label (only if this story touches `form_pages.gleam`'s resend area — it does, for the new confirmation pages).
+
+### Does NOT own
+- **The sweep** (T0/T+24h/T+48h/…/T+144h cadence, `next_attempt_at` processing) → **rc3-5**.
+- **Applicant correction-link email + `corrected_email`/`corrected_phone` re-queue** → **RC3.6 / RC4.3** (v1 correction is landlord-driven per §8.3; no `correction_token` column exists — it was deliberately omitted). rc3-4's wrong-person route only *moves to `awaiting_correction` and stops*; it does NOT email the applicant.
+- **Fraud-signal computation** (`form_session.*`, AD-10) → **rc3-7**. rc3-4 reads `_focus_seconds` at submit and stamps `submitted_at`/`form_opened_at` deltas into the result's `form_session` block as the inputs rc3-7 will build on, but does not compute line-type/DB-reuse signals.
+- **Manual / Wizard-of-Oz recording** (`channel:"manual"`, AD-8) → **RC5.1**.
+- **Landlord reference-panel display** (the `reference_calls[]` data contract, the "Contact details didn't work" state) → **RC4**.
+- **Inbound email-reply objection** (flagged reply → `objected`) → inbound-email story; the objection *handler* this story writes is the single writer both will call.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epics RC3.4, A-register applied)
+
+**AC1 — Submit (deterministic result + guarded transition + one-submission)**
+> **Given** a completed form POST to `/reference/:token` on a live row (`status='contact_initiated'`, not expired) with all required answers valid and the abuse posture (honeypot + timing) clean
+> **When** the POST runs
+> **Then** the `ReferenceCallResult v1` is structured deterministically (AD-9): `schema_version:"refcall-v1"`, `channel:"form"`, the `verification` block with per-slot variants (A9), `free_text_signals` verbatim, deterministic `ai_summary` with completeness-derived `confidence`, and the `compliance` block
+> **And** a guarded `UPDATE ... WHERE id=$1 AND status='contact_initiated'` transitions the row to `form_completed` (outcome `form_completed`); a 0-row result stands down (AD-14)
+> **And** `result` + denormalised `fraud_signals` are written; `purge_after` is stamped from the application's `retention_due_at` when set, else NULL (§9.3); `submitted_at` is stamped; the audit terminal entry is written (AD-16)
+> **And** `reference_completed` dispatches (copy per §7.9; late-completion-after-handoff copy when `taken_over_at` is set, §8.6)
+> **And** the §6.5 thank-you screen renders (identical for every completion path — the referee is never told the landlord took over, §8.6)
+
+**AC2 — One submission only (AD-3)**
+> **Given** a token whose row is already `form_completed` (or any terminal)
+> **When** a second POST to `/reference/:token` (or GET) arrives
+> **Then** the branded "already completed" state page renders (the existing `view_completed`/state-classifier path); nothing is re-persisted
+
+**AC3 — Decline (refused, §4.6 result, reference_declined)**
+> **Given** `GET /reference/:token/decline` on a live row
+> **When** rendered
+> **Then** the decline page shows the optional one-line reason field (never required) + confirm
+> **Given** `POST /reference/:token/decline` (reason optional, abuse posture clean) on a live row
+> **When** the POST runs
+> **Then** a guarded transition sets `status='refused'`, `outcome='refused'`, writes a §4.6 result (outcome + attempts, null `verification`), NULLs `next_attempt_at`, dispatches `reference_declined`
+> **And** the §10.2 decline confirmation renders; all messages stop
+
+**AC4 — Objection via stop-link (sticky objected, Art 21 evidence, AD-6/AD-14)**
+> **Given** `GET /reference/:token/stop` on a live (or terminal) row
+> **When** rendered
+> **Then** a pre-fetch-safe confirm page renders ("Stop all contact about this reference? [Confirm stop]"); **the GET mutates nothing** (link scanners prefetch — a GET that objected would silently opt out referees who never tapped)
+> **Given** `POST /reference/:token/stop` (abuse posture clean) on a live row
+> **When** the POST runs
+> **Then** a guarded transition sets `status='objected'` (sticky terminal, AD-14), NULLs `next_attempt_at`, a `reference_objection_log` row is written **at objection time** by the objection handler alone (`channel:'web'`, `objected_at`=tap time, `payload_ref`→captured web-request evidence), `reference_objected` dispatches
+> **And** the §10.2 objection confirmation renders
+> **And** a re-tap (POST on an already-terminal token) renders the branded terminal page (the guarded UPDATE is a no-op; the objection_log is written at most once per objection — see Dev Notes)
+
+**AC5 — Objection stickiness vs late events (the load-bearing edge case, AD-6/AD-14)**
+> **Given** a row already in `objected`
+> **When** a late event arrives — a second stop POST, a (future) bounce webhook, a (future) sweep tick, even a submit POST
+> **Then** the row stays `objected`; no writer moves it. The objection is non-recoverable.
+
+**AC6 — Wrong-person (awaiting_correction, no resend, AD-7)**
+> **Given** `POST /reference/:token/wrong-person` (abuse posture clean) on a live row
+> **When** the POST runs
+> **Then** a guarded transition sets `status='awaiting_correction'`, NULLs `next_attempt_at` (never a re-send to the same details — the sweep will not touch it), renders the §10.2 wrong-person confirmation
+> **And** no notification fires (the landlord sees the state in RC4); no applicant correction email (landlord-driven v1)
+
+**AC7 — Abuse posture on every public POST (AD-15)**
+> **Given** any of the five POST routes (submit/decline/stop/wrong-person, plus the existing answer/resend)
+> **When** the honeypot is filled OR the timing is suspicious (fast floor per route, TTL-aware stale cap)
+> **Then** the POST silent-drops with fake success (the page/redirect a clean referee would see) — never an error signal. The stop POST's fake-success must NOT object (the bot learns nothing; the row is untouched).
+
+**AC8 — Route registration (the rc3-3 lens-guard's concern)**
+> **Given** the new `/reference/:token/{,decline,stop,wrong-person}` routes
+> **When** a request hits each
+> **Then** it is public (`is_public_path` True — no auth; the referee has no login), CSRF-skipped (`should_skip` True — the token IS the capability), and the token is redacted in Sentry/access-log/CSP (`redact_token_route`)
+> **And** this is **verified by tests** that exercise each route end-to-end through the full router + middleware stack (not assumed from the prefix match)
+
+**AC9 — No em-dashes in user-facing copy; SSR never requires JS**
+> **Then** zero em-dash bytes inside any user-facing string literal across `form_copy`/`form_handler`/`form_pages`/`form_question_pages`/`result` (the rc3-2/rc3-3 convention; copy is UX-verbatim modulo the em-dash ban). Decline/stop/wrong-person reachable as plain POSTs without JS.
+
+## Route table (the router arms this story adds)
+
+| Method | Path | Handler | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| POST | `/reference/:token` | `form_handler.handle_submit` | the bare-token submit (the form's own action); lives above the `GET /reference/:..` catch-all |
+| GET | `/reference/:token/decline` | `form_handler.handle_decline_get` | optional-reason confirm page |
+| POST | `/reference/:token/decline` | `form_handler.handle_decline_post` | → `refused` |
+| GET | `/reference/:token/stop` | `form_handler.handle_stop_get` | pre-fetch-safe confirm (mutates nothing) |
+| POST | `/reference/:token/stop` | `form_handler.handle_stop_post` | → sticky `objected` + objection_log |
+| GET | `/reference/:token/wrong-person` | `form_handler.handle_wrong_person_get` | confirm page |
+| POST | `/reference/:token/wrong-person` | `form_handler.handle_wrong_person_post` | → `awaiting_correction` |
+
+All seven arms ride the existing `["reference", ..]` prefix match in `is_public_path`, `csrf.should_skip`, and `redact_token_route` (verified by AC8 tests; no per-arm registry edits).
+
