+-- RC3.4: extend reference_objection_log.channel to include 'web'.
+--
+-- The 2026-08-08 amendment (AD-6) moved the SMS objection trigger from an
+-- inbound STOP-reply webhook to a token-gated stop-link web route
+-- (/reference/:token/stop), which writes the Art 21 evidence row with
+-- channel: 'web' (cleaner evidence than an SMS reply: logged, timestamped,
+-- token-bound). The amendment updated architecture §4.1's channel-enum doc
+-- but the 20260731222000_create_reference_call.sql migration's CHECK
+-- constraint lagged behind it (still 'form','sms','email').
+--
+-- Expand-only: 'web' is added; existing rows are unaffected (no value is
+-- removed or narrowed). Idempotent — DROP IF EXISTS + re-ADD, so re-running
+-- against a DB that already has the wider constraint is a clean no-op
+-- (the previous revision's image keeps working against the new schema).
+ALTER TABLE reference_objection_log
+  DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS reference_objection_log_channel_check,
+  ADD CONSTRAINT reference_objection_log_channel_check
+    CHECK (channel IN ('form','sms','email','web'));
